    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "## Problem\n\nInsert-mode completion (`insexpand.c`) keeps its positions as plain integers (`compl_col`, `compl_lnum`, …) and treats them absolutely: the leader is `w_cursor.col - compl_col`, it repositions\nwith `w_cursor.col = compl_col`, and it deletes/reads the original text at `compl_col`.\n\nSo any edit (e.g., multicursor cascade) that shifts the primary's text without going through completion corrupts it. A same-line insert before `compl_col`, or a line insert above `compl_lnum`.\n\nMulticursor live-preview has to either do a bunch of internal (redundant) housekeeping to workaround that, or detect the situation and disable live-preview: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41730 .\n\n# Proposal\n\nTrack ins-completion positions with extmarks (or make them splice-aware), so text shifting before the completion keeps `compl_col`/`compl_lnum` valid. The module already keeps `compl_orig_extmarks` for undo...\n\nExpected outcomes:\n- Multicursor (insert-mode) can live-mirror before-primary shifts. Only a preview that truly overlaps (conflicts) `compl_lnum` would still need to defer.\n- Drop/simplify the conflict-detection logic in `mc_ins_cascade()` (see TODO there) and the all-or-none skip..",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
